{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_182","type":"reasoning","text":"The sealed commit b99736c1c added only the SHA256SUMS and acceptance json. So artifacts/comms wasn't committed (gitignored or not relevant). Fine.\n\nNow, for running harness validate (full) and comms, I need a git repo. Let me set up a temporary git repo, run the checks, then remove it. But comms:replay writes artifacts/comms/current-metrics.json — a new untracked artifact. Historical run presumably had artifacts/comms too but it's ignored? Let me check .gitignore for artifacts/comms. Let me grep .gitignore for 'comms'.\n\nActually earlier the agent dir doesn't have artifacts/comms. The reference worktree: does it have artifacts/comms? If gitignored, the trial diff wouldn't include it. Let me check .gitignore.\n\nTo minimize workspace pollution, I can run comms:replay with COMMS_OUTPUT_DIR pointing to a temp dir outside the workspace. The script supports `process.env.COMMS_OUTPUT_DIR`. And comms:compare reads current-metrics.json from outputDir — so I'd set COMMS_OUTPUT_DIR to the same temp dir. \n\nSo:\n- COMMS_OUTPUT_DIR=<temp> node scripts/comms/replay.mjs\n- COMMS_OUTPUT_DIR=<temp> node scripts/comms/compare.mjs\n\nFor harness validate/run I need git. Let me set up temp git.\n\nPlan:\n1. Stash my 5 new files to temp.\n2. git init -b main; git add -A; commit; update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main HEAD.\n3. Restore 5 files (untracked).\n4. Run: harness validate --spec ... ; harness run --spec ... --dry-run ; comms replay+compare with temp output.\n5. rm -rf .git; verify.\n\nConcern: `git add -A` with node_modules junction → .gitignore has node_modules presumably. Let me check quickly, and also that .gitignore is present.\n\nLet's check .gitignore contains node_modules."}}
